WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.114
"What Are Hot Dogs and Burgers Made Of?"

00:00:07.196 --> 00:00:09.920
What is in the hot dogs we eat?

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.200
A forensic study published

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.520
in the Annals
of Diagnostic Pathology

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.760
found bone, blood vessels,
nerves, cartilage, and skin.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.160
But the kicker was that
the amount of actual meat

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.800
in a hot dog
was less than 10 percent.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.040
But, of course,
the component of hot dogs

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.800
we should most care about
is the cancer risk,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.040
and it contributes
to colorectal cancer,

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.840
the number one cancer killer
of nonsmokers.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.160
That's why the prestigious
World Cancer Research Fund

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.320
and the American Institute
for Cancer Research

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.920
recommended
in their landmark report

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.880
that people simply avoid
processed meat.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.280
The National Cattlemen's
Beef Association

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.720
chided the expert report
as "bad advice,"

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.520
saying that a different report
found no link

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.880
between meat and cancer.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.840
A report that was,
in their words, "comprehensive"

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.320
by "independent scientists."

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.160
"How could the World Cancer
Research Fund research report

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.160
come to such a different
conclusion is perplexing,"

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:10.160
the beef association wrote.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.720
But I found
that so-called "independent,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.760
comprehensive review"

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.520
the beef industry
was referring to,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.920
and be perplexed no more!

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.440
I was on it like brown on rice.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.800
Let's compare.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:23.920
The report funded

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.400
by a leading nonprofit
cancer research organization

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.800
took nine independent teams
of about 200 scientists

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.920
covering nearly 7,000 studies,

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.200
compiled by some of the top
cancer researchers in the world

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.480
and overseen by the likes

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.720
of the Food and Agriculture
Organization

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.720
of the United Nations

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.880
and the World Health
Organization,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.800
producing a report
more than 500 pages long.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.720
On the other hand,
this one was 2.5 pages,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.400
written by a for-profit,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.200
scientists-for-hire
consulting firm,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.120
defenders of Big Tobacco

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.840
and virtually
every other toxic substance.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.480
And this quote-unquote
"independent" study?

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.360
Bought and paid for

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.800
by the National Cattlemen's
Beef Association.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.960
If you think
that took chutzpah,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.680
wait until you see
what the pork industry did.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.000
Smithfield, the largest
pork producer in the world,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.280
launched the "Deli for the Cure"
campaign,

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.680
donating five cents
for every pound sold

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.800
of exactly the type of meat
found most causal for cancer.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.320
What about burgers?

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.400
Anatomic pathologists
at the Cleveland Clinic

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.480
dissected fast-food burgers
to see what was inside.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.960
Americans eat
five billion burgers a year,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.400
and most consumers presume
that the hamburgers they eat

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.120
are composed primarily of meat.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.440
But what did
the researchers find?

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.400
They analyzed burgers

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.840
from eight different
fast-food joints

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.120
and found them to contain

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.240
much of the same tissues
seen in hot dogs.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.160
That's probably
not a good sign.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.000
And two of the eight
fast-food burgers

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.760
contained parasites.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.840
A quarter of the sample burgers
they looked at

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.400
had swarms
of these little parasites.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.080
And researchers found
blood vessels,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.520
nerves, cartilage.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.880
What about actual meat?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.320
What percentage
of a fast-food burger

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.840
is actually muscle flesh,

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.400
as opposed to these
other tissues, and parasites,

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.480
and fillers,
and everything else?

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.160
Meat content in the hamburgers

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.520
ranged from 2 percent
to 14.8 percent.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.360
Just two percent meat?

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.480
They're practically vegetarian!

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.120
Part of that other 85
to 98 percent

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.840
that was not muscle meat
may be ammonia.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.720
Thanks to some excellent
investigative reporting,

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.520
we learned that a company
developed a novel technique

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.920
for killing fecal bacteria:

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.800
injecting beef with ammonia.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.120
The meat industry loved
this method so much,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.720
ammonia found its way
into the majority

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.360
of hamburgers sold
across the United States.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.080
The ammonia doesn't have to be
listed as an ingredient

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.800
because it's considered
a "processing aid."

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.120
In the U.S., it made its way
into all the big chains,

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.400
and millions of pounds
every year

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.640
were given to our kids
at school.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.680
This is what the process
looks like,

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.200
producing what
one microbiologist

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.800
with the U.S. Department
of Agriculture

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.400
called pink slime,
saying he doesn't

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.680
even consider the stuff
to be meat.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.080
Not even good enough
for prisoners in Georgia.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.080
It was sent back
because the meatloaf stank

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.920
like window cleaner.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.320
Why would we feed this
to schoolchildren?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.400
School lunch officials said
they ultimately agreed

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.080
to use the ammonia-treated meat

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.280
because it shaved
about three cents off the cost

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.600
of making a pound
of ground beef.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.840
The process is banned
in Canada.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.840
Production and consumption
of pink slime

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.120
is strictly prohibited
in Europe.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.440
In the United States, however,

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.960
the meat industry sued ABC News
for its story about it,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.200
and though ABC News maintained

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.600
that its reporting
was accurate,

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.880
ABC News backed down
after facing the potential

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.920
for billions of dollars
of damages.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:56.320
And upon industry request,
the USDA simply reclassified

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.200
the product
as 100% ground beef,

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.878
displaying the raw power
of Big Slime.

